Prompt 



BUILD A FULLY FUNCTIONAL FINANCIAL AI APPLICATION: ETHICALVEST AI
1. YOUR ROLE
Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, financial-data engineer, AI engineer, UX/UI designer and application security engineer.
Build a complete, functional, polished application called EthicalVest AI.
Do not build only a static dashboard, wireframe, Figma-style mock-up or presentation. Build a working end-to-end system with real interactions, a persistent database, functioning calculations, configurable ethical screening, source-grounded generative AI, data validation, error handling and automated tests.
If an external API or API key is unavailable, implement a clearly labelled demo mode using a realistic, internally consistent sample dataset. Never pretend demo data is live or verified real-world data.
The application is a decision-support prototype for a hypothetical charitable investment scenario. It is not a trading platform, does not execute trades, and must not claim to provide regulated financial advice.
2. PRODUCT VISION
EthicalVest AI helps charitable organisations investigate whether potential investments align with their ethical investment policies while considering financial risk, cost, diversification, liquidity, investment objectives and data quality.
The application should combine:
Publicly available financial and sustainability information.
Official charity investment policies.
Official fund documents and company-holdings disclosures.
A deterministic Python-based ethical screening engine.
Transparent financial comparison and portfolio calculations.
Generative AI that explains findings using verified, traceable evidence.
A human-review and audit system.
The key product principle is:
Rules determine compliance. Python calculates numbers. Evidence supports claims. The LLM explains results. Humans retain decision-making authority.
Never delegate mandatory compliance rules, financial arithmetic or final investment decisions entirely to an LLM.
3. TARGET USERS
Design the application primarily for:
Charity trustees and investment committees.
Responsible-investment researchers.
Analysts evaluating ethical investment candidates.
Students demonstrating responsible AI in financial services.
The first deployment is a hackathon prototype. Optimise for reliability, explainability, clarity and a polished live demonstration rather than enterprise-scale infrastructure.
4. RESEARCH CASE STUDY AND DEMO DATA
Use Joseph Rowntree Charitable Trust as a research case study, subject to using its actual published documents and accurately representing their contents.
Official policy reference:
https://www.jrct.org.uk/finance-and-investment
Do not imply that the trust is a customer, has authorised the application or has approved any proposed portfolio.
Create a clearly labelled hypothetical client profile:
Name: Ethical Investment Charity — Demonstration Profile
Starting budget: £100,000
Currency: GBP
Purpose: Illustrate how a charity might assess investment candidates against documented ethical restrictions and financial requirements.
All configurable investment requirements must be editable. Do not automatically assume that every policy requirement of the real charity applies to the hypothetical client.
If the actual policy cannot be retrieved, ask the user to upload the policy or use clearly labelled illustrative rules.
Use a small, verified initial dataset of approximately 5–10 candidate funds where possible. Store actual source documents, identifiers, publication dates and evidence. If the necessary fund data cannot be verified, use clearly labelled synthetic records for software testing.
Never invent a real fund's holdings, fees, performance, sustainability rating, risk score or regulatory status.
